      "writtenOn": "2025-05-12T20:40:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for putting this together. I have mostly cosmetic comments and a few other questions / comments:\n\n- did a tool group the x86 intrinsics headers (`emmintrin.h`, `smmintrin.h`, etc.) separately or was that manually done?\n- I don\u0027t see any files targeting platforms other than x86; most importantly, that probably means the Arm NEON files could use some work",
      "revId": "43a6d2d76434986ae818effc20ac8c1ac2310c2e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f1098f4d_0466074f",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 4056663
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-05-13T07:53:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I manually grouped and sorted headers. Unfortunately, the code-base is not clang-format clean yet, so I couldn\u0027t just run clang-format over everything. So hand-modifying the files it was ...\n\nThe clang-tidy I rand on an x86 machine, so the compilation database generated by cmake was essentially choosing compilation flags and config entries. So Arm-releated compilations probably still need to be considered separately.",
      "parentUuid": "1a15fa5e_e1972f46",
      "revId": "43a6d2d76434986ae818effc20ac8c1ac2310c2e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
